---
description: Develop a dietary-aware menu and reconcile exact kitchen production before chef review.
args:{ sourceRecord: MenuProject; sourceEvidence: EvidenceItem[];ledger:KitchenLedger;change:string[];checkpoint:KitchenCheckpoint}
returns:KitchenProposal
---
Read `venueId`, `creativeBrief`, `ingredientInventoryIds`, `serviceWindow` and `chefOwnerId` from the top level of the MenuProject record. Use its food-safety and service constraints to govern each proposed dish and substitution; no generic recipe may override them. Carry every source fact and evidence ref into the analysis branch that depends on it; when any transformed proposal conflicts with this anchor, hold that branch for review instead of accepting the placeholder.

Bind requirements = `interpretKitchenBrief(ledger.brief, change, ledger.ingredientFacts, sourceRecord, sourceEvidence)`. Keep mandatory restrictions distinct from preferences. Bind candidateDishes = `designDishConcepts(ledger, requirements)`; reject any proposed substitution whose verified ingredient facts do not cover the exact restriction.

Bind composition = `composeServiceMenu(ledger, requirements, candidateDishes)`. Treat each shared sauce or prep component as one production node while retaining links to every dish. Bind batchAudit = `reconcileKitchenBatches(ledger, composition.dishes)` to recompute exact quantities from the actual selected production recipes and exact cover count, then compare each dish, ingredient, unit and quantity with the persisted batch artifact. Do not treat `ledger.exactScaledBatches` as proof of its own correctness. If any discrepancy or arithmetic blocker exists, preserve supplied and recomputed values, mark affected dishes blocked, and require an approved recipe correction or documented rounding rule; do not silently replace production quantities. Bind scaledBatches = batchAudit.supplied. Bind resourceCheck = `scheduleKitchenLine(ledger, composition.sharedPrep, composition.dishes)`; overlapping use of a limited station is infeasible and must be replanned.

Bind tasting = `propagateTastingRevisions(ledger, change, composition, resourceCheck)`. Separate subjective preferences from repeatable defects; a changed shared component invalidates all dependent dishes and disclosures. Bind safetyReview = `verifyIngredientAndServiceControls(ledger, requirements, tasting, scaledBatches, batchAudit)`. An allergen-free label requires verified venue controls plus qualified approval. Bind proposal = `assembleKitchenProposal(ledger, checkpoint, composition, tasting, scaledBatches, safetyReview)`. The returned proposal is the durable kitchen result: preserve the supplied checkpoint's cost figure unless a verified cost artifact is present, advance revision lineage from the actual selected dishes and ingredient lots, and carry all prior invalidated dish IDs forward with the tasting invalidations. Return proposal, including its complete updated checkpoint; do not claim food safety or release from recipe composition alone.
